    what: "M3.5 (#395): a Tool Forge crossbow -- iron rod body, iron limb, iron binding, string -- drawn and still holding its charge, after three shots. The `forgeweave:crossbow_loaded` component is the new format: upstream 1.12's CrossBow keeps its `TAG_Loaded` NBT boolean and nothing else (no stored ammo -- the arrow is found and spent at fire time), so this is a bare byte, and a crossbow that survives a hotbar swap or a save/reload has to still be loaded when it comes back. The rest is what the crossbow's own part shape pins: a `tool_materials` whose `handle` is the tough rod that is simultaneously the tool's EXTRA (Role.CROSSBOW_BODY -- upstream's PartMaterialType.crossbow names HANDLE and EXTRA), and a `launcher_stats` whose bonus damage carries CrossBow#buildTagData's closing `data.bonusDamage *= 1.5f` (iron's 7.0 -> 10.5). ForgeBowGameTests#crossbowStatsMatchUpstream assembles this exact crossbow at a real Tool Forge and asserts the same numbers."
}
